 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "Here's the point.",
   "start": 0.725,
   "end": 1.887
  },
  {
   "text": "Each wave grows like x to the power of its zero's real part.",
   "start": 1.887,
   "end": 5.913
  },
  {
   "text": "A zero on the line makes a wave that grows like root x.",
   "start": 5.913,
   "end": 9.688
  },
  {
   "text": "A zero at three quarters would make one growing like x to the three quarters:",
   "start": 9.688,
   "end": 14.05
  },
  {
   "text": "far louder.",
   "start": 14.05,
   "end": 15.15
  },
  {
   "text": "So the Riemann Hypothesis says the error in counting primes stays as small as it",
   "start": 16.1,
   "end": 20.15
  },
  {
   "text": "possibly can: about root x, up to logarithms.",
   "start": 20.15,
   "end": 24.113
  },
  {
   "text": "That's the typical drift of a random walk of x coin flips.",
   "start": 24.113,
   "end": 27.788
  },
  {
   "text": "Assuming RH, there's even an explicit bound on the gap between pi of x and L I of",
   "start": 27.788,
   "end": 32.75
  },
  {
   "text": "x, from x equals 2657 on.",
   "start": 32.75,
   "end": 36.463
  },
  {
   "text": "Up to a million, the primes stay inside it.",
   "start": 36.463,
   "end": 39.325
  }
 ],
